                "value": ""
              },
              {
                "name": "opc-request-id",
                "value": ""
              }
            ],
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "esxiHostId",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path",
                "description": "The [OCID](/Content/General/Concepts/identifiers.htm) of the ESXi host.\n"
              }
            ]
          },
          "docs": "Deletes the specified ESXi host. Before deleting the host, back up or\nmigrate any VMware workloads running on it.\n\nWhen you delete an ESXi host, Oracle does not remove the node\nconfiguration within the VMware environment itself. That is\nyour responsibility.\n\n**Note:** If you delete EXSi hosts from the SDDC to total less than 3,\nyou are still billed for the 3 minimum recommended EXSi hosts. Also,\nyou cannot add more VMware workloads to the SDDC until it again has at\nleast 3 ESXi hosts.\n\nUse the ["
        },
